          "path": "_m/g/b/v/n/mount-edgcumbe-country-park-wp/camellia-woodland-geograph-org.jpg",
          "filename": "Camellia Woodland - geograph.org.uk - 348346.jpg",
          "caption": "Camellia Woodland. It's an overcast grey February day, raining off and on.  It's in the middle of bare deciduous woodland whose branches and twigs will occasionally release large drops of water onto your head just to remind you that it will rain again soon.  In the middle of this scene these foreign interlopers, camellia bushes, are exploding with a riot of colour.  Here's a close up of one of the flowers from the nearest bush 347687.",
          "alt": "Camellia Woodland. It's an overcast grey February day, raining off and on.  It's in the middle of bare deciduous woodland whose branches and twigs will occasionally release large drops of water onto your head just to remind you that it will rain again soon.  In the middle of this scene these foreign interlopers, camellia bushes, are exploding with a riot of colour.  Here's a close up of one of the flowers from the nearest bush 347687.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 514,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Tony Atkin",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Camellia_Woodland_-_geograph.org.uk_-_348346.jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "mount-edgcumbe-country-park-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "gbvn",
          "smallPath": "_m/g/b/v/n/mount-edgcumbe-country-park-wp/camellia-woodland-geograph-org-small.webp"
        },
        {
          "path": "_m/g/b/v/n/mount-edgcumbe-country-park-wp/camellias-behind-mount-edgcumb.jpg",
          "filename": "Camellias behind Mount Edgcumbe House - geograph.org.uk - 347649.jpg",
          "caption": "Camellias behind Mount Edgcumbe House. Camellias are an early flowering shrub and the mild weather this winter has brought them out particularly early, unfortunately mild weather is accompanied by strong winds and almost continuous rain which does not help to show off the blooms at their best, however not all the camellias at Mount Edgcumbe are in such an exposed position and there are plenty more to find.  Here are some close up photos of the blossom: 347682, 347685, 347687.",
          "alt": "Camellias behind Mount Edgcumbe House. Camellias are an early flowering shrub and the mild weather this winter has brought them out particularly early, unfortunately mild weather is accompanied by strong winds and almost continuous rain which does not help to show off the blooms at their best, however not all the camellias at Mount Edgcumbe are in such an exposed position and there are plenty more to find.  Here are some close up photos of the blossom: 347682, 347685, 347687.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 427,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Tony Atkin",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Camellias_behind_Mount_Edgcumbe_House_-_geograph.org.uk_-_347649.jpg",
